{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/415223-idigam-chronicle-themes-and-possibilities-question","id":415223,"title":"Idigam Chronicle themes and possibilities question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-22T09:10:06-08:00","id":415223,"title":"Idigam Chronicle themes and possibilities question","content":"So, admittedly not that familiar with WtF in general but would be interested in getting the Idigam Chronicles when it comes out to expand a bit on possible plays with the Werewolf theme. The thing is though that &quot;spirit cops&quot; theme doesn't sound that interesting to me personally especially since it, in a way, is already present in WtA with which I have plenty of experience. So I am asking you the fans of WtF here, and especially those who are familiar with both WtF and WtA, about the other themes especially those separating it from Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> I would be most interested in the possibility of portraying Lycanthropy as more of a Curse than a calling to become a spirit cop, or a warrior of Gaia/Wyrm as was the case with WtA, and Idigam Chronicle, or 2nd ed WtF did it by the way have a project name like Blood &amp; Smoke had other than the Idigam Chronicle, seem to have at least some of that Curse thought present in that one can become Wolf Blooded through bite or encounter with a Werewolf but does this theme go further? Can one use this upcoming version of Werewolf to portray them as more Cursed lineages that struggle with their bestial sides and perhaps an instinct to hunt, rather than some legacy of spirit guardianship bestowed upon them. I guess, from the Idigam being front and center here as antagonists, that it would be hard to separate them completely from any spirit world stuff, a clear legacy of WtA, and focus completely on the Curse aspect at least without some serious re-writing of the whole setting. But keeping the spirit side could it be played as I suggested without too heavy modifications?<br /> <br /> And in general what other themes you feel are most important in it besides the Spirit Cop thing which comes up a lot, so much in fact that cop shows are recommended over Werewolf films as inspiration on other threads here.<br /> <br /> I am asking this because I would be interested to get a fresh look at the Werewolf mythos but considering how many good books Onyx Path is spitting out currently, and I still have a few that are already out that I should get as well, I need to pick and choose which ones to get and which ones to leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T09:31:50-08:00","id":415320,"title":"","content":"Think less spirit cop, more half-spirit. Your inner wolf spirit longs to roam the shadow, to hunt and to claim a territory of its own. Despite your fleshy human body, you can't deny this instinct. Oh you can try, but eventually the wolf will find its way out, and when that happens it won't be pretty if you've denied it for so long. Those tragic &quot;cursed&quot; werewolves who massacre their own villiages are the ones who try to deny what they are. The only way to prevent that is to embrace the wolf. But be careful too not to lose yourself to it, lest you start to fade away and become not but a spirit, devoid of any thought save the hunt. It's about maintaining harmony within <i>yourself</i>. Yes, guarding your territory is part of that, but that makes you no more a spirit cop than a wolf is an animal cop for fending off other predators from its hunting grounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-22-2015, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T09:36:51-08:00","id":415324,"title":"","content":"Major revision: the theme of the game is hunting, so while spirit cop is a thing you can be, the game feels more to me like primal beast. Like the horror movies and novels made into a table top game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 02-22-2015, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T09:39:40-08:00","id":415326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/415223-idigam-chronicle-themes-and-possibilities-question?p=415320#post415320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think less spirit cop, more half-spirit. Your inner wolf spirit longs to roam the shadow, to hunt and to claim a territory of its own. Despite your fleshy human body, you can't deny this instinct. Oh you can try, but eventually the wolf will find its way out, and when that happens it won't be pretty if you've denied it for so long. Those tragic &quot;cursed&quot; werewolves who massacre their own villi ages are the ones who try to deny what they are. The only way to prevent that is to embrace the wolf. But be careful too not to lose yourself to it, lest you start to fade away and become not but a spirit, devoid of any thought save the hunt. It's about maintaining harmony within <i>yourself</i>. Yes, guarding your territory is part of that, but that makes you no less a spirit cop than a wolf is an animal cop for fending off other predators from its hunting grounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope there is a paragraph similar to this in Werewolf: Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T10:06:34-08:00","id":415344,"title":"","content":"Yeah that's written a lot better then my rambling","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T10:10:03-08:00","id":415347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/415223-idigam-chronicle-themes-and-possibilities-question?p=415326#post415326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really hope there is a paragraph similar to this in Werewolf: Second Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>As do I. The new approach to Harmony was what won me over on Forsaken, which I always wanted to like but couldn't quite get into in 1e. Werewolves are a big contender for my favorite monsters, but I never saw the themes I like from them in 1e (largely because they had been cribbed by Requiem with the Beast). But then 2e comes along and not only brings those themes into the game, but improves on them by adding an opposite extreme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T12:00:41-08:00","id":415508,"title":"","content":"I like the new approach to Harmony as well. The whole &quot;spirit cops&quot; thing never settled well with me \u2014 if anything, it sounds like something wereDOGS might be assigned too. Wolves are important to the ecosystem and the trophic changes in it, and the domino effect of a hunter doing its thing seems far more interesting in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T12:37:53-08:00","id":415550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/415223-idigam-chronicle-themes-and-possibilities-question?p=415347#post415347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As do I. The new approach to Harmony was what won me over on Forsaken, which I always wanted to like but couldn't quite get into in 1e. Werewolves are a big contender for my favorite monsters, but I never saw the themes I like from them in 1e (largely because they had been cribbed by Requiem with the Beast). But then 2e comes along and not only brings those themes into the game, but improves on them by adding an opposite extreme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly why the 2ed also sell me on, when 1ed could not. At least from the blog post, this incarnation feel more primal, more direct, and hunting focused than policing the Shadow - because it's not the only thing it's connected to. Of course, those themes are still here, but new Harmony could work as system for great &quot;cursed beast&quot; stories, as well as &quot;man hunting even for his family&quot;. And I now have idea for Predator King werewolf that is primal hunter by nights, when he leave his home every day to leave his 9-year old daughter after she goes to sleep. Adding new Gift system that highlights Uratha as &quot;slasher-like&quot; figures, with <i>human</i> emotions, and not only spirit bans placed on them.<br /> <br /> Not too mention as to making the Humans favorite Prey of Iron Masters - with all that we get back in part to the &quot;human side&quot; of <i>half-human, half-spirit</i> of gameline equation. And it makes me very happy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T16:40:47-08:00","id":415826,"title":"","content":"The theme of the first edition was never &quot;spirit cops&quot;. It was savage fury. I don't know how it's been run in other tables, but my characters had to witness an entire world that wanted to see them dead, skinned and eaten (and if you were very, very lucky, in that order). It's the outrage building up? How about when the lesser predators, which aren't normally a rival to you pick on your (oblivious) loved ones and wear their skin like sock puppets, sometimes devouring their brain or hearts in the process? How about when a far numerical superior fanatical, inhumane cult of your same species comes down howling for your blood for the alleged sins of your forebears, after you swore to at least two spirit Gods that you wouldn't murder your spiritual kin?<br /> <br /> Cops must answer to due process. The Forsaken only have to uphold a nebulous oath which they themselves will never reach an agreement over it's interpretation.<br /> <br /> Cops don't make the laws. Forsaken are the masters of their territories, if they manage to bend the spirit wilds to their wills.<br /> <br /> Sometimes perps slip thru the cracks on account of technicalities. Your prey won't have a lawyer ensuring a fair trial as it's thorn apart by your fangs and claws.<br /> <br /> I guess that the only question that really matters is... <b>When will you rage?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T16:47:43-08:00","id":415832,"title":"","content":"Yes, 'spirit cops' is just a lazy label to explain it that caught on and never left. They do patrol to keep the two worlds apart but there's a lot more to them than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T22:27:51-08:00","id":416167,"title":"","content":"It's also about the horror of the First Change at first, an experience that usually ends with the werewolf tearing apart people close to him. After that, as werewolves begin to settle into their lives as Forsaken (if they're lucky enough - many aren't), there's plenty of horror in the dawning understanding of the worldview upon the world of Werewolf: the Forsaken is based - a nightmare of the real world in which the aphorism &quot;might makes right&quot;, that's pretty much a reality in the world we live in, is taken to its logical conclusion; in which humans have no power and no promise of safety at any time, and in which this thing people call a &quot;life&quot; is just a product of incredible chance in the face of impossible adversity of powerful forces to which humans serve no purpose other than as discardable energy source and mobile transportation.<br /> <br /> And in addition to that, there's getting used to the werewolf condition, the rage, the territorial urges - towards people, even. You would think people have it bad when Shadow things take over. Werewolves take the way vampires objectify people to a different level, trading and fighting over wolf-blooded as breeding stock the way people would barter over dogs. And that's the protagonists of the setting.<br /> <br /> Once the PCs have made contact with the Pure - or maybe a lot sooner, all it takes it to meet Forsaken werewolves of certain lodges - the Storyteller gets to introduce the horror of mindsets as extreme as to put one's dogma over one's own life and that of other people. The Pure have a Plan, and there's nothing they wouldn't do to achieve it, and no sacrifice too great and no atrocity too revolting. And there are plenty of people like that in the real world, people who put their extreme beliefs ahead of their own existence - suicide bombers and the like; but that doesn't make the Pure's actions less of a mockery of the self-sacrifice of the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> There is a more direct sort of horror in Werewolf. I've never been hunted by my life before, but there have been a one or two situations in which people chased me through the streets, wanting to beat me up. And it's worse than being in a fistfight, because those are over soon. Being chased can go on and on .. and this is an immovable part of life as a Forsaken werewolf. Their enemies are legion. Werewolves don't get to retire from their life and say &quot;screw this, I'm doing something else.&quot; The Hunt is all they will and can ever have.<br /> <br /> All that remains, then, is to introduce the Bale Hounds, werewolves sworn to the darkest of spirits - a pledge that should begin to make perfect sense and seem like the only logical option left, because who doesn't like to be on the winning team?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:18:52-08:00","id":416247,"title":"","content":"Something else of note (while I'm thinking clearly and have more than 4 hours of sleep) is the religious ideologies of the tribes. The Tribes of the moon and the pure (and the Bale hounds for that matter) are separated less by blood and more by religious beliefs of the world. Everything can be a truth or a lie. All spirits lie. Every story starts with &quot;this story is true.&quot; While the tribes as described in 1e have a decidedly apocalypse feel, they are fundamentally different. They are still tribes as tribes can be described, and that is not to say that there isn't still full blood lines of werewolves and wolf blooded, but the basis for their tribes come down to beliefs and personal mantras over blood lines and duties. <br /> <br /> Ugh I'm a terrible seller these days! (and i work retail presently!!) To answer your earlier question (Which I failed to do horrendously), yes, you can play them however you want, and portray them however you want. You'll find the community in this particular forum to be incredibly helpful in molding rules and lore to assist you in such a game where you want it to be a curse. Hell most if not all of us Cahalith players here are stoked for the new auspice set up as it makes us more like the American Werewolf in London, and far far less the twilight beast.<br /> <br /> If you have any questions on how best to make such a game happen (cause lets face it, we're all getting 2e one way or another!) ask away here! Lord knows Wyrdhamster abuses the hell out of it! Kidding ofcourse hamster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T07:01:24-08:00","id":416459,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your answers everyone.<br /> <br /> There are still certain concerns of too much similarity with Apocalypse, especially the slogan above of &quot;When will you Rage?&quot; which has been an Apocalypse stable for over 20 years now. And unfortunately for my ears Christian A, your post sounds in way to many ways to resonate with the Apocalypse but I do hope it's just me.<br /> <br /> Still Lyrics of War since you seem to share some love with my favourite Apocalypse Tribe I assume you have had the chance to compare the two games at length and seem to be of the mind that 2nd edition of WtF will be it's own thing, and I do like the way Charlaquin represented Harmony which I believe has changed somewhat from 1st ed and the WtA/WtF conversion guide. I do think I'll have to cough up the money some where to get the 2nd edition even if I need to fiddle with a few things to get it to work, still it sounds it's more geared toward the Cursed aspect than Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> All in all I am pleased if the Spirit Cop thing is downplayed, even though cop series were still recommended watching for WtF feel on this forum, even if I am slightly saddened that they went with the half-spirit theme again, though changing that wouldn't have been an option for 2nd edition the chance should have been made when developing the 1st edition, but I can live with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T07:34:22-08:00","id":416483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/415223-idigam-chronicle-themes-and-possibilities-question?p=416459#post416459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are still certain concerns of too much similarity with Apocalypse, especially the slogan above of &quot;When will you Rage?&quot; which has been an Apocalypse stable for over 20 years now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I don't get that. It's pretty easy to predict when you'll become susceptible to death rage, and the tagline for Werewolf the Forsaken seems to be 'The Wolf Must Hunt.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T07:40:55-08:00","id":416492,"title":"","content":"The new 2e Death Rage is quite a different animal to its earlier form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T08:37:04-08:00","id":416512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/415223-idigam-chronicle-themes-and-possibilities-question?p=416459#post416459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And unfortunately for my ears Christian A, your post sounds in way to many ways to resonate with the Apocalypse but I do hope it's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who has been playing Apocalypse for 15 years, no idea how you came to that conclusion. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T09:10:52-08:00","id":416532,"title":"","content":"I can see it actually, in the over themes. So apocalypse feels like listening to black metal and punching walls yeah? Forsaken feels like watching event horizon. The focus on existence is bigger then in apocalypse, where you play a martyr for the greater good (or evil as my chronicle is going). In forsaken it's just about you being the wolf, coming to terms with it. It's not about frenzy checks, it's about avoiding death rage, keeping yourself in balance. Thank god the harmony system has changed to reflect the dual nature better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T10:43:30-08:00","id":416642,"title":"","content":"Apocalypse is <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=CEDKcEPDQO4\" target=\"_blank\">Of Wolf and Man</a>. It's about primal rage, fighting a war you know you've lost, and embracing the righteous indignation that knowledge fuels. (SHAPESHIFT!) You know this world is ending, and there's nothing you can do to stop it. (SHAPESHIFT!) But you'll be damned if you aren't at least going to go down in a blaze of fucking glory (BACK TO THE MEANING, back to the meaning of LIFE!)<br /> <br /> Forsaken is <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=JZweDwbJ_Ic\" target=\"_blank\">Howl</a>. It's about the irresistable need to hunt. You are not a creature of this human society. (Now there's no holding back.) You are an animal that longs to stalk the primal wilds, to feel the anticipation of the hunt, the thrill of the chase, the pride of the kill. (I'm making to attack.) You have a life, a family, friends, a job, you can't just leave it all behind. (My blood is singing with your voice, I want to pour it out.) But all of that ceases to matter as soon as you see your Auspice moon, the glorious face of mother Luna shining down on you, and reminding you that you are a wolf and the wolf MUST hunt. (The saints can't help me now, the ropes have been unbound, I hunt for you with bloody feet across the hallowed ground, and HOWL!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-23-2015, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T14:12:40-08:00","id":416875,"title":"","content":"I feel I should mention some of em have red brands instead of silver and aren't feeling the moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}